{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Honor your father</b> is juxtaposed to <b>the Sabbath</b>, for regarding the Sabbath too it is written וכבדתו — that one must honor it with food and clothing." "<b>ולמען ייטב לך</b> Tagin on the טי\"ת — for his mother carried him 9 months, and his father and mother were careful regarding the 9 traits enumerated in Nedarim. Their mnemonic is אסנ\"ת משגע\"ח — notarikon: בני אנוסה, בני שנואה, בני נדה, בני תמורה, בני מריבה, בני שכרות, בני גרושת הלב, בני ערבוביא, בני חצופה. That is: בני אנוסה — need not be that he raped a woman and begot a son from her; rather even if she is his wife and he forced her to intercourse. And so we learned in tractate Kallah: Why are children born to a man with blemishes? Because he demands and his wife is not willing to him — meaning, she does not acquiesce to him. Rabbi Yehudah says: because she says to him at the time of intercourse 'I am forced' — and א\"ב רוצ' ואינה רוצה. And so it is in Eruvin: whoever forces his wife to a matter of mitzvah is called a sinner, as it says גם בלא דעת נפש לא טוב — one finds that intercourse by force is forbidden even with one's wife; but if he needs that act, he should placate her and afterward lie with her. בני שנואה — literally, that she is hated at the time of intercourse; but if she is desired at the time of intercourse, even though she is hated, it is permitted. בני נדה — even though he is not a mamzer by Torah law; and some say that one of them was in a state of ban prohibiting intercourse, and the same applies if one of them is a mourner. בני תמורה — that he intended for another forbidden relation and his wife happened to be available; and some say even if both are his wives, that he intended for this one and another happened to be available. בני מורדת — she said to him 'I do not want you,' yet nevertheless he has intercourse with her, and she is to him like a harlot, even if she consented. And according to another version: בני מריבה — that they quarrel with each other every time, so that this intercourse is like harlotry, since it is not from love. בני שכרות — that he or she is drunk. בני גרושת הלב — that in his heart he intends to divorce her, even if there is no hatred in his heart, such as those whom the court forces to divorce and he has resolved in his heart to divorce her, and afterward has intercourse with her. בני ערבוביא — that he has intercourse with his wife and sets his mind on another, even if both were his wives. בני חצופה — that she demands him verbally, and she is like a harlot and it is forbidden to maintain her. But one whose wife entices him with words of affection and adorns herself before him so that he sets his mind on her — of her the Sages said that wise and understanding children come forth from her, like Leah from whom Issachar came forth. And all these 9 traits, even if they do not need to fulfill the commandment of procreation, such as if she is pregnant — nevertheless in all these traits the child is blemished and is called a rebel. And one must honor them with 9 things: feeding, clothing, and so forth, as stated in the first chapter of Kiddushin. 17 extra words in the latter Decalogue compared to the former, equal to the numerical value of טוב. And this is what is written here למען ייטב לך — for these are not in the former." "<b>כאשר צוך ה' אלהיך</b> — ס\"ת in gematria: מרה." "<b>על האדמה וגו'</b> — and juxtaposed to it is <b>לא תרצח</b>, because it is written ולארץ לא יכופר לדם."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The text shifts between בני מורדת and בני מריבה as alternate versions of the fourth item; both preserved as in the source. אצ\"ל expanded as 'need not be' following the logical flow. א\"ב resolved as abbreviation for רוצה ואינה רוצה based on context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:09.730294337Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}